The UE may accept the following EMM messages without NAS integrity protection, but only in the applicable exceptional procedure/state (e.g. no valid EPS NAS security context, emergency services procedure):

- **ATTACH ACCEPT** — in an emergency attach case;
- **ATTACH REJECT**;
- **TRACKING AREA UPDATE ACCEPT** — in a tracking-area update for emergency bearer services;
- **TRACKING AREA UPDATE REJECT**;
- **SERVICE REJECT**;
- **AUTHENTICATION REQUEST**;
- **AUTHENTICATION REJECT**;
- **IDENTITY REQUEST**; and
- **EMM INFORMATION**.

Outside the specified exceptions, a UE discards NAS messages that are not integrity protected.

Examples include receipt of network NAS messages that trigger an EMM common procedure, such as:

- an **AUTHENTICATION REQUEST** (authentication procedure);
- an **IDENTITY REQUEST** (identification procedure);
- a **SECURITY MODE COMMAND** (security mode control procedure);
- a **GUTI REALLOCATION COMMAND** (GUTI reallocation procedure); and
- an **EMM INFORMATION** message (EMM information procedure).

Received NAS/AS information and local events (for example, timer expiry or a change in available security context) can also determine whether such a procedure is initiated.

Upon receiving the **DEREGISTRATION ACCEPT** message, the UE shall delete any stored:

- 5G-GUTI;
- last visited registered TAI;
- TAI list;
- allowed NSSAI;
- configured NSSAI;
- mapping of allowed NSSAI; and
- rejected NSSAI, if any.

When the UE requests both MICO mode with active time and eDRX, the network can decide to:

- accept MICO mode with active time and eDRX;
- accept MICO mode with active time and reject eDRX;
- reject MICO mode with active time and accept eDRX; or
- reject both MICO mode with active time and eDRX.

The UE shall delete the stored 5GMM context, i.e.:

- the **5G-GUTI**;
- the **TAI list**;
- the **allowed NSSAI** and any **mapping of allowed NSSAI**;
- the **configured NSSAI** and any **mapping of configured NSSAI**;
- the **rejected NSSAI** (if present);
- the **list of equivalent PLMNs**; and
- the **UE security context** (including the ngKSI).

This applies for the relevant access type when the DEREGISTRATION REQUEST carries the specified abnormal 5GMM causes and indicates **“re-registration not required.”**

Upon reception of an **RRCReject**, the UE shall:

- stop timer **T300**;
- if `waitTime` is included, start timer **T302** with the received value;
- enter **RRC_IDLE**; and
- perform cell selection in accordance with **TS 38.304**.
